// Maple Bay — RELATIONSHIPS: the romance track, person by person (A)  (src/story/rel_hearts_a.js)     PURE DATA. No init().
// Marlow, Nico, Tasha, Imani, Felix. (Noor, Tav, Haru, Celeste, Barnaby: rel_hearts_b.js. The shared track: rel_romance.js.)
//
// HEART  { person, title, premise, thread, scenes: Scene[11], vows: string[], livein: { morning[], evening[], chores[], night[] },
//          kind: { letdown: Step[], breakup: Step[], after: string[] } }
// SCENES, always in this order (tools/rel_check.mjs insists on all eleven):
//   meet      the moment something is noticed, in the world (Friend, 40+). Sets nothing by itself; it makes "Say how you feel" natural.
//   h1 h2 h3  the HEART SCENES: their own story, a piece at a time. h1 at Dating, h2 at Together, h3 at Partner. Invitations; never expire.
//   steady    their answer to "Ask where this is going"        -> Together
//   partner   their answer to "Ask to be partners"             -> Partner
//   keys      the key exchange
//   movein    their answer to "Ask them to move in"
//   proposal  their answer to "Propose"                         -> Engaged
//   m1 m2     married life
//   Scene = _rel_kit V(): { id '<person>.<key>', title, when, place, invite, window, steps, fx, ask?: [question, answer] }
//   `ask` is the remembered thread: after the scene the verb "Ask about..." offers the question, and they give the answer.
// =============================================================================
